# .obsidian/plugins/.gitignore
# Track plugin configurations for reproducibility while protecting secrets

# ============================================================================
# Plugin Code: Now TRACKED for persistence across clones/pulls
# ============================================================================
# Previously ignored *.js and *.css but this caused plugins to not persist
# after git operations. Now tracking them for reliability.
#
# NOTE: This increases repo size but ensures plugins work immediately.
# ============================================================================
*.exe

# ============================================================================
# ALWAYS IGNORE: Cache Files
# ============================================================================
**/cache.json
**/cache/

# ============================================================================
# Plugin-specific secrets are managed by .gitignore files in each plugin folder
# ============================================================================
# The following plugins have their own .gitignore to protect data.json:
#   - copilot (OpenAI/Anthropic/Google API keys)
#   - obsidian-local-rest-api (API key, private key, certificates)
#   - obsidian-imgur-plugin (Imgur client ID, album IDs)
#   - smart-connections (AI service API keys)
#   - readwise-official (Readwise API token)
#   - obsidian-raindrop-highlights (Raindrop API token)
#   - github-copilot (GitHub auth tokens)
#   - google-drive-sync (OAuth tokens)
#   - obsidian-google-lookup (Google API key)
#   - medium-importer (authentication tokens)
#   - obsidian-raindrop (Raindrop API token)
#   - obsidian-git (askpass script)

# ============================================================================
# TRACKED BY DEFAULT: All other data.json files are tracked
# ============================================================================
# Safe configurations that should be version controlled:
# - templater-obsidian/data.json (folder templates)
# - obsidian-git/data.json (commit messages, preferences)
# - todoist-sync-plugin/data.json (UI preferences, token stored separately)
# - calendar/data.json (UI preferences)
# - terminal/data.json (terminal profiles)
# - metadata-menu/data.json (field definitions)
# - lazy-plugins/data.json (plugin load order)
# - obsidian-plugin-groups/data.json (plugin groups)
# - etc.
